Z||000000||wxxo||01-04-2001||03:09 PM||||well its time to replace the clutch in my 86 se (yep v6 4 speed). i replaced the tranny a while back so i pretty much know what im doing except what parts to buy and where to buy them. i dont need anything special and dont want to spend a ton of cash. ive bought stuff from autozone before but it really didnt seem to be too great quality you know. anyhow i know i need a pressure plate, throwout bearing, clutch disk and probably a flywheel shim. (by the way what is that stuff called that you use when putting the bolts back into the flywheel?) also anyone who knows of an easy way to do this please let me know. when i swapped trannys it took a very long time. i didnt even drop the cradle either. took it out from the side. anyhow thanks very much in advance for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shaft||01-04-2001||03:41 PM||||I'm a co-op for LuK Clutches and I would suggest looking into one of the RepSets they sell. The RepSet comes with everything you'll need to replace you clutch (include clutch, disc, release bearing, pilot bearing/bushing, spline tool and lubricant). If you talk to the people at the aftermarket center (or a local shop that carries LuK parts) they should be able to tell you everything that is included in the kit and they should be able to hook you up with whatever you need. I don't know the number to call but the website is <A HREF="http://www.lukclutch.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lukclutch.com/</A>  <P>Although I have not used a LuK clutch yet I have tested them at the plant and I can assure you that the quality is good and you'll be very satisfied with their customer service. If you have questions about how a LuK clutch performs in a Fiero I'd ask Tina. She mentioned before that there was one in her car. I'd help you out with a discount, but being a co-op I only get one clutch at a discout and I'm saving that one for me.<p>[This message has been edited by Shaft (edited 01-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||01-04-2001||03:46 PM||||LuK clutch sets came factory in  all manual tranny Fieros.<P>LocTite?<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero Fanatic||01-04-2001||04:26 PM||||It's possible to replace to clutch without dropping the cradle.||||reg||1
